course: dictionary
lesson: 14098
title: One word, many meanings: men
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Men» is the plural of «man». One man, two men, three men. When you read «men», look at the words around it to see which meaning fits. «Three men carried the sofa up the stairs» means three adult males.
explain: «The captain and his men set sail at dawn.» Here «men» means the crew, the people working under the captain. The clue is the word captain, because a captain leads a group of workers or soldiers.
explain: Old books sometimes use «men» to mean all people: «all men are created equal». The clue is that the sentence is about everyone, not just boys or men. Today many people prefer «people» or «everyone», so you will mostly see the first meaning in everyday writing.
explain: In games, the pieces in draughts are called men: «Move your men forward, one square at a time.» The clue is the game. Always ask what the sentence is about, then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: «Men» is the plural of «man».
fact: «Men» can mean adult male people, soldiers or workers under a leader, or pieces in some games like draughts.
fact: «Men» can also mean all people in old-fashioned writing, but many people now say «people» or «everyone» instead.
fact: «Men's» with an apostrophe shows that something belongs to men, as in «the men's team».
fact: «3 men can paint a fence in 6 hours» is a maths problem about how fast people work.
exercise: What is the plural of «man»? | *men | mens | mans | manny
exercise: «The captain and his men set sail at dawn.» What does men mean here? | *soldiers or workers under a leader | adult male people only | all people in the world | pieces in a game
exercise: Find and copy the word that means more than one man. | mend | man | *men | mean
test: «All men are created equal.» What does men mean in this old-fashioned sentence? | only adult male people | pieces in a game | soldiers under a leader | *all people
test: In «the men's toilets», what does the apostrophe show? | many men are missing | *the toilets belong to men | the word is spelled wrong | there are two men
exam: «3 men can paint a fence in 6 hours.» What kind of problem is this? | a problem about how many men are in a team | a problem about which men are the best painters | *a problem about how fast people work | a problem about how tall the fence is
